<title>EGYPT: Egypt crude, natgas output slides lower in May.</title>
<headline>Egypt crude, natgas output slides lower in May.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian crude oil production fell for the third consecutive month in May to an average 836,452 barrels per day (bpd) from 838,666 bpd in April, the state-owned Egyptian General Petroleum Corp (EGPC) said on Sunday.</p>
<p>EGPC said natural gas output also fell to 1.319 billion cubic feet a day from 1.337 billion cubic feet in April.</p>
<p>Condensates were lower in May at 39,323 bpd compared to 39,267 bpd while butane and propane output was higher at 31,580 bpd from 31,500 bpd in April.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
